{"key": "07cdd556abdcda1d67805fdf0b31273da9e9452a", "outputs": ["```python\n    logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    logger.setLevel(logging.DEBUG)\n\n    formatter = logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    console_handler = logging.StreamHandler()\n    console_handler.setFormatter(formatter)\n\n    logger.addHandler(console_handler)\n\n    data = request.json\n    logger.debug('Received data: %s', data)\n\n    return data\n```", "```python\n    import logging\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/log')\n    def log():\n        '''\n        Log data from request and return it.\n        '''\n        # Get the incoming request data\n        data = request.get_json()\n        \n        # Log the received data\n        logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n        \n        # Return the received data\n        return data\n```", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n    \n    # Get data from request\n    data = request.get_json()\n    \n    # Log the data\n    logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n    \n    # Return the data\n    return data\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure basic logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\n    # Get data from request\n    data = request.json  # Assuming JSON input\n\n    # Log the data\n    logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n\n    # Return the received data\n    return data\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\n    try:\n        # Get data from request\n        data = request.json or request.args.to_dict()\n\n        # Log the data\n        logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n\n        # Return the data\n        return data, 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Log the error\n        logging.error(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n        return {\"error\": str(e)}, 500\n```", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    # Get data from request\n    data = request.get_json()\n\n    # Log the data\n    logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n\n    # Return the data\n    return data\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG, format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    try:\n        # Extract data from request\n        data = request.json\n        if not data:\n            raise ValueError(\"No data provided\")\n\n        # Log the data\n        logging.debug(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n\n        # Return the data\n        return data, 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Log errors\n        logging.error(f\"Error processing request: {str(e)}\")\n        return str(e), 500\n```", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    # Get request data\n    request_data = request.args.to_dict() if request.method == 'GET' else request.json\n\n    # Log the request data\n    for key, value in request_data.items():\n        logging.info(f'Received: {key} = {value}')\n\n    # Return the request data as JSON\n    return request_data\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\n    # Get data from request\n    data = request.get_json() if request.is_json else request.form.to_dict()\n\n    # Log data\n    logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n\n    # Return the data as a response\n    return data\n```", "```\nimport logging\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/log')\ndef log():\n    '''\n    Log data from request and return it.\n    '''\n    # Configure logging\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n    \n    # Get request data\n    data = request.json or request.form.to_dict()\n    \n    # Log the data\n    logging.info(f\"Received data: {data}\")\n    \n    # Return the data as a response\n    return data\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "3356b20fbb5732528565a7556261740e46c6a28e", "outputs": ["from jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader\n    import os\n\n    # Load the template\n    env = Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader('../assets/templates'))\n    template = env.get_template('template.html')\n\n    # Get param from request\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n\n    # Replace the placeholder in the template\n    rendered_template = template.render(param=param)\n\n    return make_response(rendered_template)\n```<|/assistant|>", "from flask import render_template\n\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n\n    if not param:\n        return make_response(\"No parameter provided\", 400)\n\n    with open('../assets/templates/template.html', 'r') as file:\n        template = file.read()\n\n    replaced_template = template.replace('{{param}}', param)\n\n    return render_template_string(replaced_template)\n```<|/assistant|>", "from flask import Flask, request, make_response\nimport os\nfrom jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\napp.config['TEMPLATES_AUTO_RELOAD'] = True\n\nenv = Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), 'templates')))\n\n@app.route('/template_replaced', methods=['GET'])\ndef no_template_engine_replace():\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n    if not param:\n        return make_response(\"Parameter 'param' is missing\", 400)\n    \n    template = env.get_template('../assets/templates/template.html')\n    rendered_template = template.render(param=param)\n    \n    response = make_response(rendered_template)\n    response.mimetype = 'text/html'\n    return response\n```<|/assistant|>", "from flask import render_template_string\n    from pathlib import Path\n\n    # Load the template file\n    template_path = Path('..') / 'assets' / 'templates' / 'template.html'\n    with open(template_path, 'r') as file:\n        template = file.read()\n\n    # Get the parameter from the request\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n\n    # Replace the placeholder in the template with the parameter\n    rendered_template = template.replace('{{ param }}', param)\n\n    return make_response(rendered_template, 200)", "```python\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n    if not param:\n        return make_response(\"Parameter 'param' is missing.\", 400)\n\n    with open('../assets/templates/template.html', 'r') as file:\n        template = file.read()\n\n    replaced_template = template.replace('{{param}}', param)\n\n    response = make_response(replaced_template)\n    response.mimetype = 'text/html'\n    return response\n```<|/assistant|>", "return \"No template engine replacement\"", "from jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader\n    import os\n\n    env = Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader('../assets/templates'))\n    template = env.get_template('template.html')\n\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n    if not param:\n        return make_response(\"Param 'param' is missing\", 400)\n\n    replaced_content = template.render(param=param)\n    response = make_response(replaced_content)\n    response.mimetype = 'text/html'\n    return response\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n    if not param:\n        return \"Param 'param' is missing\", 400\n\n    with open('../assets/templates/template.html', 'r') as file:\n        template_content = file.read()\n\n    replaced_template = template_content.replace('{{param}}', param)\n\n    response = make_response(replaced_template)\n    response.mimetype = 'text/html'\n\n    return response\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    param = request.args.get('param')\n    with open('../assets/templates/template.html', 'r') as file:\n        template = file.read()\n        rendered_template = template.replace('{param}', param)\n    \n    response = make_response(rendered_template)\n    return response\n```<|/assistant|>", "from jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader, TemplateNotFound\n    import os\n\n    template_dir = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '../assets/templates')\n\n    env = Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader(template_dir))\n    \n    try:\n        template = env.get_template('template.html')\n        param_value = request.args.get('param_name')  # Replace 'param_name' with the actual parameter name from your URL\n        rendered_template = template.render(param=value)\n        response = make_response(rendered_template)\n        response.headers['Content-Type'] = 'text/html'\n        return response\n    except TemplateNotFound:\n        response = make_response(\"Template not found\", 404)\n        response.headers['Content-Type'] = 'text/plain'\n        return response\n</|assistant>"]}
{"key": "2c0932b03671af45fc9ba13b103700cef87503c7", "outputs": ["from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = re.compile(r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)')\n    if pattern.search(query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'", "from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = re.compile(r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)')\n    \n    if pattern.search(query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'", "from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)'\n    \n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```", "from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = re.compile(r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)')\n    if pattern.search(query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'", "from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = re.compile(r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)')\n    \n    if pattern.search(query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '').strip()\n    pattern = r'(www\\.example\\.com/)|(beta\\.example\\.com/)'\n    \n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```\n```", "from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    \n    pattern = r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = re.compile(r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/')\n    \n    if pattern.search(query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n\n    if not query:\n        return 'No query provided', 400\n\n    patterns = ['www.example.com/', 'beta.example.com/']\n\n    for pattern in patterns:\n        if re.search(pattern, query):\n            return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    \n    return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```\n```", "from flask import request, Flask\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/search')\ndef search():\n    query = request.args.get('query', '')\n    pattern = r'(www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/)'\n    \n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```"]}
{"key": "88bd2e8f35a545c6b826fb01840fa0ca390f0042", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\nimport os\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\napp.config['UPLOAD_FOLDER'] = '../assets/img'\n\n@app.route('/img/upload', methods=['POST'])\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.form.get('filename')\n    img_data = request.form.get('img')\n\n    if not filename or not img_data:\n        return Response(\"Invalid input\", status=400)\n\n    try:\n        # Decode the base64 image data\n        img_bytes = base64.b64decode(img_data)\n        \n        # Save the image to the specified folder\n        img_path = os.path.join(app.config['UPLOAD_FOLDER'], f\"{filename}.png\")\n        with open(img_path, 'wb') as img_file:\n            img_file.write(img_bytes)\n        \n        return Response(f\"Image uploaded successfully as {filename}.png\", status=200)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error uploading image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.args.get('filename')\n    img_param = request.args.get('img')\n    \n    if not filename or not img_param:\n        return Response(\"Invalid request\", status=400)\n    \n    try:\n        decoded_img = base64.b64decode(img_param)\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(decoded_img)\n        return Response(\"Image uploaded successfully\", status=200)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error uploading image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload', methods=['POST'])\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.form.get('filename')\n    img_base64 = request.form.get('img')\n\n    if not filename or not img_base64:\n        return Response(\"Invalid request\", status=400)\n\n    try:\n        img_bytes = base64.b64decode(img_base64)\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(img_bytes)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error uploading image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n\n    return Response(\"Image uploaded successfully\", status=200)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.args.get('filename')\n    img_param = request.args.get('img')\n\n    if not filename or not img_param:\n        return Response(\"Filename or img parameter is missing\", status=400)\n\n    try:\n        decoded_img = base64.b64decode(img_param)\n        with open(f\"../assets/img/{filename}.png\", 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(decoded_img)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error uploading image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n\n    return Response(status=200)\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/img/upload` that accepts two parameters: `filename` and `img`. It uses these parameters to upload an image file to the specified path in the `assets/img` directory. The image is expected to be provided in Base64 format. If the parameters are missing or an error occurs during the upload process, appropriate responses are returned.", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.args.get('filename', default='default.png')\n    img_param = request.args.get('img', default='')\n\n    if not img_param:\n        return Response(\"No image provided\", status=400)\n\n    try:\n        decoded_img = base64.b64decode(img_param)\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as img_file:\n            img_file.write(decoded_img)\n        return Response(\"Image uploaded successfully\", status=200)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error uploading image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.form.get('filename')\n    img_param = request.args.get('img')\n    \n    # Decode the base64 string\n    img_data = base64.b64decode(img_param)\n    \n    # Save the image to the file\n    with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n        f.write(img_data)\n    \n    return Response(status=200)\n```<|/assistant|>", "from flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    '''\n    Get the \"filename\" from the request and the \"img\" parameter from the request.\n    Use base64 to decode the \"img\" parameter.\n    Then, save the image to the file \"../assets/img/{filename}.png\"\n    :return: a Response with status code equals to 200.\n    '''\n    filename = request.args.get('filename')\n    img_param = request.args.get('img')\n\n    if not filename or not img_param:\n        return Response(\"Missing filename or img parameter\", status=400)\n\n    try:\n        # Decode the base64 string\n        img_data = base64.b64decode(img_param)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error decoding base64 image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n\n    try:\n        # Save the image to the specified file path\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(img_data)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error saving image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n\n    return Response(status=200)", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload', methods=['POST'])\ndef upload_img():\n    if 'filename' not in request.form or 'img' not in request.form:\n        return Response('Missing required parameters', status=400)\n    \n    filename = request.form['filename']\n    img_base64 = request.form['img']\n    \n    try:\n        # Decode the base64 string\n        img_bytes = base64.b64decode(img_base64)\n        \n        # Save the image to the file\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(img_bytes)\n        \n        return Response(status=200)\n    \n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f'Error uploading image: {str(e)}', status=500)\n```\n\nThis code defines a route `/img/upload` that accepts POST requests. It expects two form parameters: `filename` and `img`. The `img` parameter is expected to be a base64-encoded string of the image data. The function decodes the base64 string, saves it to a file in the `../assets/img/` directory, and returns a 200 OK response. If any errors occur during this process, a 500 Internal Server Error response is returned with an error message. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.args.get('filename')\n    img_param = request.args.get('img')\n    \n    if not filename or not img_param:\n        return Response(\"Missing parameters\", status=400)\n    \n    try:\n        img_data = base64.b64decode(img_param)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error decoding base64 image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n    \n    try:\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(img_data)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"Error saving image: {str(e)}\", status=500)\n    \n    return Response(\"Image uploaded successfully\", status=200)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport base64\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/img/upload')\ndef upload_img():\n    filename = request.args.get('filename')\n    img_base64 = request.args.get('img')\n\n    if not filename or not img_base64:\n        return Response(status=400)\n\n    try:\n        img_binary = base64.b64decode(img_base64)\n        with open(f'../assets/img/{filename}.png', 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(img_binary)\n\n        return Response(status=200)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(str(e), status=500)\n```\n\nThis code defines a route `/img/upload` in a Flask application that handles image uploads. It expects the `filename` and `img` parameters in the request. The `img` parameter is expected to be a base64-encoded string of the image data. The function decodes the base64 string to binary, saves it to a file in the `../assets/img/` directory, and returns a response with a status code of 200. If any errors occur during the process, a response with a status code of 500 is returned. <|/assistant|>"]}
